    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "malloc — a memory allocator",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_322_02\" id=\"tag_17_322_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/stdlib.h.html\">stdlib.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nvoid *malloc(size_t</tt> <i>size</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_322_03\" id=\"tag_17_322_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]malloc[/I5]() function shall allocate unused space for an object whose size in bytes is specified by [I6]size[/I6] and whose\nvalue is unspecified.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The order and contiguity of storage allocated by successive calls to [I7]malloc[/I7]() is unspecified. The pointer returned if the\nallocation succeeds shall be suitably aligned so that it may be assigned to a pointer to any type of object with a fundamental\nalignment requirement and then used to access such an object in the space allocated (until the space is explicitly freed or\nreallocated). Each such allocation shall yield a pointer to an object disjoint from any other object. The pointer returned points\nto the start (lowest byte address) of the allocated space. If the space cannot be allocated, a null pointer shall be returned. If\nthe size of the space requested is 0, the behavior is implementation-defined: either a null pointer shall be returned, or the\nbehavior shall be as if the size were some non-zero value, except that the behavior is undefined if the returned pointer is used to\naccess an object.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "For purposes of determining the existence of a data race, [I8]malloc[/I8]() shall behave as though it accessed only memory\nlocations accessible through its argument and not other static duration storage. The function may, however, visibly modify the\nstorage that it allocates. Calls to [A9][I10]aligned_alloc[/I10]()[/A9], [A11][I12]calloc[/I12]()[/A11], [A13][I14]free[/I14]()[/A13], [I15]malloc[/I15](), [S16][[A17]ADV[/A17]][/S16] [IMG18] &nbsp;[A19][I20]posix_memalign[/I20]()[/A19], [IMG21]\n\n[S22][[A23]CX[/A23]][/S22] [IMG24]\n[A25][I26]reallocarray[/I26]()[/A25], [IMG27]\n&nbsp;and [A28][I29]realloc[/I29]()[/A28] that allocate or deallocate a particular region of memory shall\noccur in a single total order (see [A30][I31]4.15.1 Memory Ordering[/I31][/A30]), and each\nsuch deallocation call shall synchronize with the next allocation (if any) in this order.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A9": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/aligned_alloc.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I10": {
